@baseUrl = https://localhost:7145
# Replace with IDs returned by YOUR API. questionId is an inspection snapshot ID.
@templateId = 1
@inspectionId = 1
@questionId = 1
# Copy version from GET inspection; replace after EVERY successful write.
@expectedVersion = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
# Retain an earlier version here to verify a stale edit returns 409.
@staleVersion = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 1. Start an inspection from an existing published template (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "templateId": {{templateId}},
  "siteName": "Lahore Office"
}

### 2. Read questions + current version (200). Update variables above.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}
Accept: application/json

### 3. Save an answer (200). Replace expectedVersion with returned version.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/questions/{{questionId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Pass",
  "comment": "Floors checked and clean.",
  "expectedVersion": "{{expectedVersion}}"
}

### 4. Simulate a stale screen (409): staleVersion must be an OLD nonempty version.
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/questions/{{questionId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Fail",
  "comment": "This stale write should not be saved.",
  "expectedVersion": "{{staleVersion}}"
}

### 5. Submit (200 after all required questions are answered; otherwise 409).
# Use latest expectedVersion. Fail is a completed answer, not a submission blocker.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "expectedVersion": "{{expectedVersion}}"
}

### 6. Verify Submitted status, UTC timestamp, answers and new version (200)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Try editing a submitted inspection (409)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/questions/{{questionId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Fail",
  "expectedVersion": "{{expectedVersion}}"
}

### Missing version (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/questions/{{questionId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Pass"
}

### Unknown answer (400)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/inspections/{{inspectionId}}/questions/{{questionId}}/answer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "answer": "Unknown",
  "expectedVersion": "{{expectedVersion}}"
}
